# M1 / B015 — ef-core, git-workflow.

C R186 OL GOV-015 | MUST NOT | Perform a repository-changing Git operation (commit, push, merge, rebase, reset, force-push, branch deletion and similar) only when explicitly requested, never merely because implementation is complete. | Git operations | Explicit user request.
C R187 OL GOV-019 | MUST NOT | Never discard, overwrite, reset, clean or otherwise destroy user work to make a Git operation easier; do not automatically stash, reset or discard work to make a merge or rebase proceed; do not remove a worktree that contains uncommitted user work. | Git operations | none stated
C R188 OL GOV-020 | MUST | Before a repository-changing Git operation inspect the relevant repository state (status, diff, staged diff) and use the minimum operation required; do not silently clean up unrelated working-tree changes or perform unnecessary operations such as renaming an existing user branch to satisfy a naming convention. | Git operations | none stated
C R189 OL GOV-016 | MUST | Parallel implementation streams use separate branches or worktrees; one branch is not checked out in multiple normal worktrees and each worktree stays focused on its branch's concern. | parallel work | none stated
C R190 OL WF-022 | MUST | Before committing inspect the staged diff and include only the intended logical change; do not stage unrelated files merely because they are modified; one logical change per commit with its protecting tests, no artificial tiny commits and no unrelated fixes combined. | commits | none stated
C U2 LU GOV-015,GOV-020 | MUST NOT (high-risk) | High-risk Git operations (reset --hard, clean, push --force, push --force-with-lease, branch deletion, rebasing shared history) are performed only when explicitly requested or clearly required by an approved workflow, after inspecting what will be lost or rewritten. | Git operations | Clearly required by an approved workflow. | GOV-015 requires an explicit request for repository-changing operations; whether 'clearly required by an approved workflow' is an admissible substitute for that request cannot be decided from the oracle text. | An agent could run git clean or a force-push without a direct user request when it judges an approved workflow to require it.
C X23 EX GOV-015,GOV-020 | MUST NOT | main, master and other protected or shared branches are treated as non-rewritable; a shared branch is never force-pushed unless the user explicitly requests history rewriting and the consequences are understood. | push and history rewriting | Explicit user request for history rewriting of a shared branch. | GOV-015 requires an explicit request for force-push; the oracle does not declare named branches categorically non-rewritable. | A requested force-push to main is still refused or challenged under this rule.
C X24 EX WF-009,WF-022 | MUST | Before preparing a pull request run verify; the PR has a focused purpose and its description explains what changed, why, how it was verified and important compatibility or migration notes. | pull requests | none stated | WF-009 covers truthful verification reporting and WF-022 focused commits; the oracle does not prescribe PR description contents. | A PR description listing only file names does not follow the workflow.
C X25 EX RUN-002 | MUST NOT (review defect) | Fire-and-forget EF Core asynchronous operations are a defect. | EF Core code | none stated | RUN-002 forbids blocking async I/O; the oracle does not separately forbid unawaited persistence operations. | Starting SaveChangesAsync without awaiting it is a review finding.

